<title>GERMANY: Tietmeyer - stability pact success needs commitment.</title>
<headline>Tietmeyer - stability pact success needs commitment.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank president Hans Tietmeyer on Thursday said the success of the stability pact to ensure fiscal discipline after European monetary union would depend on the level of self-commitment by nations.</p>
<p>Tietmeyer also told a news conference he would have to wait and see how &quot;self-commitment&quot; would be formulated in the legal EMU text.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
